        "text": "You are implementing ONE step of a causal-graph module in worktree isolation. Work only in your worktree; do not commit or merge.\n\n**FIRST — self-check the worktree base.** Run `git log --oneline -3` and `git branch --show-current`. You MUST see commit `0d8abb5 causal_graph Step 0: models`. Confirm `src/analysis/causal_graph/models.py` exists and exports `Node, NodeType, Graph, Family`. If that commit is absent or models.py is missing, STOP and report exactly \"WORKTREE BASE WRONG: did not branch from feature/code_trace\"; do NOT create models.py.\n\nThen implement **Step 4 — Tier-2 ops** (read plan Step 4 + design §5.2, §5.3, §3.2).\n\n**Own only:** `src/analysis/causal_graph/ops.py`, `tests/analysis/causal_graph/test_ops.py`. Touch nothing else.\n\n**Implement** the op catalog + executor. Ops are callable primitives over a `Graph`/`Family`:\n`select(type, where)`, `attr(node, key)`, `children(node)`, `parent(node)`, `neighbors(node, edge, dir)`, `descendants(node, edge, dir)` (dir=up|down), `path(a, b)`, `resolve(ref)`, `group_by(nodes, key)`, `filter(nodes, where[, unique])`, `aggregate(nodes, fn, key)` (fn=count|sum|max|collect).\n- `run_plan(family, plan, scope=\"tree\") -> result` executes a JSON list of ops left-to-right, each op reading the previous result unless it names an input. `scope` = self | tree | subagent-id (design §3.2). This is a **serialized call sequence, NOT a text language** — no parser, no eval; dispatch each `{\"op\": ...}` to a fixed handler. `where` predicates are simple dicts: `{\"is_error\": true}`, `{\"count\": {\">\": 3}}`, `{\"type\": \"turn\"}`.\n\n**Test** the three worked-example plans from design §5.3 on a hand-built `Family` fixture, asserting the documented result shapes:\n1. failed tools > 3 with errors; 2. tool most often right before an error; 3. tokens into turns touching a .md file.\nAlso: `resolve` returns None for an absent child (partial); `scope=self` excludes subagent nodes. Build the fixture so each plan has a known asserted answer.\n\nDo NOT read `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/traces` (outside the worktree). Run `venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/analysis/causal_graph -q`.\n\n**Repo rules:** Python 3.11+, tests via `venv/bin/python -m pytest`, no `git -C`, NEVER reference Claude/Claude Code in code/comments/output. Report git self-check output, files changed, assertions + results, and any op-semantics assumptions (esp. how \"loop prev\" is resolved). Do not commit or merge.",
